[h1]Phobos Exchange[/h1]
[b]Version:[/b] 0.2.1
[b]Publication status:[/b] Not published - held draft, awaiting owner gameplay checks

Every hold you fill and every shortage you fly into moves somebody's share price. The Lodestar Exchange puts the system's companies on your wrist: watch them on the long hauls, buy on the way up, sell before the turn.

[h2]What it does[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]An EXCHANGE app[/b] on the PDA home screen. Tap it and the PDA closes and the Exchange panel opens.
[*][b]Eight listed companies[/b]: the game's own Smartlink, Testudo, Ayotimiwa Corp. and the Green Energy Company, Brightvein Mining and Coldwell Volatiles, and Verdemorrow and Halewright, the makers of Phobos equipment.
[*][b]Prices from the game's cargo markets[/b]: each company follows a few named stations. When weapons run short at Port Yangshan, Smartlink climbs; when ore piles up at Zhonghuamen Terminal, Brightvein slides.
[*][b]Trends that last weeks[/b]: the whole market, each sector and each company rise and fall in phases you can see on the chart, and shares creep upward over the years.
[*][b]Charts[/b] over 3 days, 120 days or 2 years, with your alerts and what you paid marked.
[*][b]Buy and sell for cash[/b], with the cost worked out before you confirm. The spread, a small commission and the push of a big order mean quick round trips lose.
[*][b]Price alerts[/b] that go off once when a price reaches your level, even through a time skip.
[*][b]The market wire[/b]: big moves and turns, each with its cause, in the crew log. After a long absence, one summary.
[*][b]Your shares[/b]: value, cost and gain for each holding, and Sell everything.
[*]Two years of price history from the moment you first open it.
[*]In the F3 console, phobosexchange quotes, quote, buy, sell, holdings, alert, alerts, sellall, drivers and state.
[/list]

[h2]List your own companies[/h2]
The company list is a data file. Add companies and sectors, or change what each one follows, in BepInEx/config/PhobosExchange/exchange, or ship them in an add-on. A built-in guard refuses any company whose shares would earn more on average than a loan costs. Stories can move prices: a company's news, set off by a story, lifts or sinks its price once, and the exchange tells stories when you buy in, hold a large stake or sell out. An example add-on lists a company of its own with its own story.

[h2]Fair warning[/h2]
[list]
[*]Shares earn a few percent a game year on average, less than a Phobos Banking loan costs. Borrowing to sit on shares loses money; reading the board and timing it is where the profit is.
[*]A moment always has the same price however you got there, through watching, fast play or a skip, and a reload never rerolls it.
[*]Test commands that change your save are locked until the game's own unlockdebug, warn every time and need confirm.
[*]The cover is original promotional artwork, not an in-game screenshot.
[/list]

[h2]Requirements[/h2]
[list]
[*]Ostranauts 1.0.1.5, BepInEx 5 and Phobos Framework 0.129.0 or newer.
[*]BepInEx 5 through EddieSM / EsMM27's [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3741030124]BepInEx Mod Loader[/url], including its one-time setup.
[*]Phobos Banking is optional: with it, the Credit overview shows what your shares are worth.
[/list]

[h2]Installing from the Workshop[/h2]
[list]
[*]Subscribe to the BepInEx Mod Loader and follow its setup instructions.
[*]Subscribe to Phobos Exchange and the Phobos items listed under Required items.
[*]Start Ostranauts once so the loader copies the plugins, then restart it once so they load. Do the same after each update.
[*]Check that the mods are enabled in the MODS screen.
[/list]

[h2]Saves and limits[/h2]
[list]
[*]One small record on your character holds the market, your shares and alerts, and the chart history. Nothing else in the save changes except your cash and the ledger lines your trades write.
[*]Sell everything before removing the mod: shares are only worth credits while the exchange can buy them back. Reinstall it and your shares are still there.
[*]The figures are invented for the game and tuned for weeks of play, not measured from any real market.
[*]Automated checks pass; in-game checks are still pending.
[/list]

[h2]Credits[/h2]
Created by Phobos A. D'thorga (phobosgekko). Independent community work, not endorsed by Blue Bottle Games or Kitfox Games. It reads the game's own station markets and writes trades to its own ledger. Smartlink, Testudo, Ayotimiwa and the Green Energy Company are the game's companies, reported on as a wire service would.
